course: dictionary
lesson: 7341
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Plastic» is one of them. The context, meaning the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning the writer chose.
explain: «Animals can get trapped in plastic rings by the neck, beak or legs.» Here plastic tells us what the rings are made of. It describes the rings, so it is an adjective: made of plastic.
explain: «Pay with plastic» is a different meaning. In shops, plastic can mean a bank or credit card. Check by swapping in another word: «pay with cards» still makes sense, so this meaning fits.
explain: Plastic can also be a noun, the material itself, as in «Plastic lasts hundreds of years». Ask yourself: is it the stuff, or is it describing something? That question will usually show you the meaning.
fact: Plastic is a light, strong material made in factories, often from oil.
fact: As an adjective, «plastic» means made of plastic, as in «a plastic cup».
fact: Plastic can also mean easy to bend and shape.
fact: In science, plastic is an insulator: it does not carry electricity.
fact: «Plastic» can mean bank or credit cards, as in «pay with plastic», which is an informal use.
exercise: «Animals can get trapped in plastic rings by the neck, beak or legs.» What does plastic tell us about the rings? | What colour they are | *What they are made of | How old they are | How many rings there are
exercise: «Heat moves slowly through insulators, such as wood, plastic, wool, cork and air.» Nadia says plastic here means a credit card. What is the better meaning? | A bank card | Something very old | A toy for children | *A material that heat moves slowly through
exercise: What does «pay with plastic» mean? | Pay by bending the plastic | *Pay with a bank or credit card | Pay in coins made from plastic | Pay with a plastic bag
test: «You should pull a plug out by holding the plug itself, not by yanking the cord, because yanking can damage the wires and break their plastic cover.» In this sentence, what is the plastic? | A bank card | A mould for shaping cups | A shopping bag | *The cover around the wires
test: «Plastic lasts hundreds of years.» What does this tell us? | Plastic is a type of food | Plastic is only used for cups | Plastic breaks down in a single day | *Plastic stays around for a very long time
exam: Which use of plastic is an adjective? | *a plastic cup | Plastic lasts hundreds of years | Pay with plastic | Plastic is an insulator
